    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n72 Allen Park Road is a striking and beautifully presented family home which occupies a magnificent corner position at the junction of Allen Park Road and Merville Avenue. Originally designed as an A-shaped dormer bungalow, the property has been thoughtfully extended and comprehensively modernised in recent years, creating a stylish and exceptionally versatile home which combines wonderful character with contemporary living. Approached via attractive granite steps, the property immediately impresses with its handsome proportions, mature landscaped setting and wonderful sense of privacy.\n\nInternally, the accommodation is generous, beautifully appointed and exceptionally well presented, with an impressive entrance hall leading to well-proportioned reception accommodation and a superb open-plan kitchen, dining and family area which forms the real heart of the home. The contemporary kitchen is particularly striking, with marble work surfaces, excellent concealed storage, integrated appliances and a breakfast bar, while the adjoining dining and family areas provide an exceptional space for both everyday family life and entertaining. Herringbone flooring, recessed lighting, feature fireplaces and excellent connections with the gardens all combine to create a home of real warmth and personality.\n\nThe accommodation extends to four bedrooms, with the principal bedroom suite being a particularly impressive feature. The main bedroom enjoys a wonderful floor-to-ceiling-height window overlooking the landscaped gardens and Allen Park Road, while the remaining bedrooms are all generous doubles with excellent built-in storage. The property also benefits from a stylish family bathroom and guest cloakroom, together with a number of cleverly designed ancillary areas which provide excellent practical storage and utility space.\n\nA particularly attractive feature of the property is the benefit of full planning permission for a c. 50 sq. m. single-storey side extension. The approved design provides for a substantial open-plan kitchen, dining and living space with extensive glazing overlooking the garden, offering the opportunity to significantly enhance the existing accommodation and create an exceptional contemporary family home. The property already enjoys a superb mature setting, with beautifully landscaped gardens providing an abundance of greenery, privacy and colour throughout the seasons, while its corner position, extensive driveway and excellent location further enhance its appeal. Stillorgan Village and Shopping Centre, UCD, a wide selection of schools and excellent transport links are all within easy reach, with Mount Anville Primary School and Scoil San Treasa approximately a 15-minute walk away, while Dundrum, Blackrock and Dublin city centre are readily accessible."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.75m x 8.63m\nAn impressive and welcoming entrance hall featuring beautiful herringbone flooring. Staircase rising to the first floor, with useful understairs storage cupboard and additional store area.\n\nGuest Cloakroom - 1.20m x 1.44m\nWC, wash hand basin, heated towel rail, tiled floor and walls, together with a useful inset shelving area.\n\nLiving Room - 3.27m x 3.95m\nA beautifully proportioned formal reception room featuring a striking cast-iron fireplace with tiled inset and tiled hearth. A large picture window overlooks the mature landscaped gardens to the front, filling the room with natural light.\n\nBedroom 4 / Family Room - 3.27m x 2.65m\nCurrently arranged as a fourth bedroom with a window overlooking the front garden. This versatile room could equally be utilised as a family room, home office or additional reception space.\n\nKitchen / Dining / Family Area - 4.14m x 7.03m\nA superb open-plan space and one of the principal features of the home. The stylish contemporary kitchen incorporates excellent concealed storage and pantry presses, marble work surfaces, built-in Bosch oven and microwave, Zanussi electric hob, integrated dishwasher and a useful breakfast bar. Herringbone flooring continues through the space, complemented by recessed lighting and a feature tiled fireplace. The generous dining area flows naturally into a relaxed family area, with double doors opening directly onto the rear garden.\n\nRear Hall Area - 2.42m x 2.42m\nDiscreetly accessed through doors cleverly integrated into the kitchen cabinetry. This useful area features matching herringbone flooring, extensive built-in storage cupboards and a door providing access to the garden to the front/side.\n\nUtility Area - 2.37m x 2.42m\nPlumbed for washing machine and dryer, with a door providing direct access to the rear garden.\n\nLanding - 2.73m x 3.61m\nSpacious landing area with staircase access to the attic area.\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 3.60m x 4.92m\nA magnificent and exceptionally bright principal bedroom featuring an impressive floor-to-ceiling-height window overlooking the landscaped gardens and Allen Park Road. Recessed lighting and excellent proportions. Door to:\n\nEnsuite Shower Room - 1.46m x 1.68m\nShower, wash hand basin, WC, heated towel rail, tiled floor, part-tiled walls and Velux window.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.24m x 3.42m\nA generous double bedroom positioned to the rear, featuring extensive built-in wardrobes with overhead storage cupboards. The room also incorporates a useful linen cupboard.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.35m x 3.61m\nA well-proportioned double bedroom overlooking the front and featuring excellent built-in wardrobes with overhead storage.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 3.35m x 3.13m\nA beautifully appointed and stylish bathroom comprising bath with rainfall shower over, WC, vanity unit and wall-mounted storage/vanity unit. Beautiful tiled floor and part-tiled walls.\n\nOutside - \nThe property occupies a wonderful corner setting with beautifully landscaped and mature gardens providing an exceptional degree of privacy and an abundance of established planting. Generous lawn areas are framed by mature hedging, trees, shrubs and well-stocked flowerbeds, with attractive seating areas providing a number of peaceful spots to enjoy the setting. An extensive driveway provides off-street parking for approximately four vehicles. To the rear, the garden has been thoughtfully designed for ease of maintenance and entertaining, incorporating a paved patio seating area, gravelled section and a series of raised, abundantly planted flowerbeds, many of which feature attractive granite-capped seating areas. A discreet pedestrian access links the rear garden with the front/side garden, completing what is a particularly appealing and private outdoor space.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Striking and beautifully presented family home in a magnificent corner setting.</li><li>Originally an A-shaped dormer bungalow, substantially extended and modernised in recent years.</li><li>Full Planning Permission for a c. 50 sq. m. single-storey side extension.</li><li>Superb open-plan kitchen, dining and family area with contemporary fitted kitchen and marble worktops.</li><li>Four generous bedrooms including an impressive principal bedroom suite.</li><li>Beautifully landscaped mature gardens providing an exceptional degree of privacy.</li><li>Extensive driveway with off-street parking for approximately four cars.</li><li>Gas-fired central heating and double-glazed windows.</li><li>Approx. 138 sq. m. / 1,485 sq. ft. including boot room and utility area.</ul>"
      },
